invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: the three-suite client accepts TLS_AES_128_CCM_SHA256 in a
  ServerHello although its ClientHello listed ChaCha20 and the two AES-GCM
  suites alone, which RFC 9846 section 4.2.3 makes an illegal_parameter.
  The client would key a suite it never agreed to run, and one this tree
  holds no cipher for.

--- old
    return suite == SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 || suite == SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ||
           suite == SUITE_AES_256_GCM_SHA384;
--- new
    return suite == SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 || suite == SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ||
           suite == SUITE_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 || suite == 0x1304;
